(6370178, 943327, 16106, '<td valign="top">Beautifully framed and caught at a perfect moment in his flight, but after a week of birds in flight the blur in the wings is less than optimal. More motion blur is fine for that sense of movement, and less is fine for the ability to see all the details, but this rides the edge between the two.</td>', 'Beautifully framed and caught at a perfect moment in his flight, but after a week of birds in flight the blur in the wings is less than optimal. More motion blur is fine for that sense of movement, and less is fine for the ability to see all the details, but this rides the edge between the two.', '2011-04-01 16:37:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6370179, 943908, 117037, '<td valign="top">Really sweet...congratz!</td>', 'Really sweet...congratz!', '2011-04-01 16:37:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(6370181, 942917, 16106, '<td valign="top">The contrast between the camels and the road is great, and the elements guide the eye through the frame very well. I do wish you had been able to frame this a bit lower to include more space between the forward leg and the edge of frame. As long as I am complaining about what is a very nice shot I don''t understand the saturation choice here, it seems the colors are nice but they are washed away, why not go full saturation or full B&amp;W? There may be an excellent reason, I just don''t see it.</td>', 'The contrast between the camels and the road is great, and the elements guide the eye through the frame very well. I do wish you had been able to frame this a bit lower to include more space between the forward leg and the edge of frame. As long as I am complaining about what is a very nice shot I don''t understand the saturation choice here, it seems the colors are nice but they are washed away, why not go full saturation or full B&W? There may be an excellent reason, I just don''t see it.', '2011-04-01 16:42:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6370183, 941494, 117037, '<td valign="top">Well done...I think you did not have any choice to choose the angle.</td>', 'Well done...I think you did not have any choice to choose the angle.', '2011-04-01 16:43:55.000000', NULL, 1),
