(6371632, 941698, 100393, '<td valign="top">I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5.<br/> <br/>I love the colours and the processing here but the clipped pedal bothered me too much to overlook. Back to bump. I was too mean.</td>', 'I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5. I love the colours and the processing here but the clipped pedal bothered me too much to overlook. Back to bump. I was too mean.', '2011-04-03 16:03:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(6371664, 942380, 108580, '<td valign="top">OK that''s just disturbing. The effect you were looking for? The imagery and post is excellent. Give Stephen King a call. He could use this as his next cover. A heart pumpin'' 8.</td>', 'OK that''s just disturbing. The effect you were looking for? The imagery and post is excellent. Give Stephen King a call. He could use this as his next cover. A heart pumpin'' 8.', '2011-04-03 16:58:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(6371693, 943717, 108580, '<td valign="top">Great study. Composition is spot on. Eyes are looking at me, sharp with the "mandatory" catch lights. Whilst I understand the "need" for catch-lights in eyes, raptors have jutting brows to specifically reduce light and shade the eyes from sun and glare. Something a lot of commentators ignore and vehemently defend that catch-lights must be visible. The black and white processing is top notch and the background is smooth and uncluttered. This is a captive bird? I think so. No matter. One of the better nature studies in this FS challenge. I might have cropped out the birds right wing (at point of carpal coverts) as it is a little distracting. 9.</td>', 'Great study. Composition is spot on. Eyes are looking at me, sharp with the "mandatory" catch lights. Whilst I understand the "need" for catch-lights in eyes, raptors have jutting brows to specifically reduce light and shade the eyes from sun and glare. Something a lot of commentators ignore and vehemently defend that catch-lights must be visible. The black and white processing is top notch and the background is smooth and uncluttered. This is a captive bird? I think so. No matter. One of the better nature studies in this FS challenge. I might have cropped out the birds right wing (at point of carpal coverts) as it is a little distracting. 9.', '2011-04-03 17:56:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6371694, 943686, 108580, '<td valign="top">Lovely lighting and wonderful processing. Crisp eyes. I might have burned the highlights on her nose a little.</td>', 'Lovely lighting and wonderful processing. Crisp eyes. I might have burned the highlights on her nose a little.', '2011-04-03 17:57:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6371696, 942710, 108580, '<td valign="top">Awesome BIF shot with perfect elements of sharpness, stop motion and composition. Perhaps a bit hot on the scapular. Great detail in the primaries. 9.</td>', 'Awesome BIF shot with perfect elements of sharpness, stop motion and composition. Perhaps a bit hot on the scapular. Great detail in the primaries. 9.', '2011-04-03 18:00:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6371698, 943176, 108580, '<td valign="top">Classic B&amp;W elephant shot emotive sky and true African grassland savannah. Wonderful composition and processing. The clear line of focus from left to right on the ellie adds punch and dimension. I would hang this on my wall.</td>', 'Classic B&W elephant shot emotive sky and true African grassland savannah. Wonderful composition and processing. The clear line of focus from left to right on the ellie adds punch and dimension. I would hang this on my wall.', '2011-04-03 18:03:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(6371700, 943988, 108580, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous landscape. Someone who knows what they are doing, both behind the lens and in the digital darkroom. You''ve chosen a perfect time of day and have handled the exposure extremely well. If it''s HDR to get the tonal range then it certainly doesn''t look it. This should be up there, at least a top 10 and maybe a ribbon. Good luck.</td>', 'Gorgeous landscape. Someone who knows what they are doing, both behind the lens and in the digital darkroom. You''ve chosen a perfect time of day and have handled the exposure extremely well. If it''s HDR to get the tonal range then it certainly doesn''t look it. This should be up there, at least a top 10 and maybe a ribbon. Good luck.', '2011-04-03 18:05:39.000000', NULL, 1),
