(6375333, 943845, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This is a complete Nixterish delight! The out-of-focus areas are fabulous, it makes for a really dynamic and actually cinematic shot. The colours are tremendous too - the deep red of the car and the various frivolity in the background.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Magnificent.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This is a complete Nixterish delight! The out-of-focus areas are fabulous, it makes for a really dynamic and actually cinematic shot. The colours are tremendous too - the deep red of the car and the various frivolity in the background. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Magnificent.', '2011-04-05 19:59:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6375335, 943607, 76335, '<td valign="top">Nicely balanced composition.</td>', 'Nicely balanced composition.', '2011-04-05 19:59:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(6375336, 943261, 76335, '<td valign="top">Processing is over the top.</td>', 'Processing is over the top.', '2011-04-05 20:00:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6375339, 939400, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Smooth and subtle. This should be boring but somehow you''ve pulled off a magic trick and made it oh so very engaging. Very little for me to comment on, so ethereal is the presentation, my brain cannot readily grapple it, the image slips from my cognition.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all<br/> <br/>Overall: Quite something from nothing. Well played.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Smooth and subtle. This should be boring but somehow you''ve pulled off a magic trick and made it oh so very engaging. Very little for me to comment on, so ethereal is the presentation, my brain cannot readily grapple it, the image slips from my cognition. Critical stuff: Nothing at all Overall: Quite something from nothing. Well played.', '2011-04-05 20:02:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6375340, 943363, 76335, '<td valign="top">Flash is a bit harsh...</td>', 'Flash is a bit harsh...', '2011-04-05 20:02:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(6375341, 941942, 76335, '<td valign="top">I do like the sepia reflection.</td>', 'I do like the sepia reflection.', '2011-04-05 20:03:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(6375344, 942838, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This is certainly bold stuff; excellent clarity and I like the way we want to get closer and look over the wall and through the glass. I like the yellow lights (?) too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: With such images I often wonder what, since the scene was there, the photographer has brought to the image... this does feel crafted though, so you must have done something. Whether it is enough is another matter.<br/> <br/>Overall: An interesting scene, well presented.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This is certainly bold stuff; excellent clarity and I like the way we want to get closer and look over the wall and through the glass. I like the yellow lights (?) too. Critical stuff: With such images I often wonder what, since the scene was there, the photographer has brought to the image... this does feel crafted though, so you must have done something. Whether it is enough is another matter. Overall: An interesting scene, well presented.', '2011-04-05 20:05:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6375345, 941519, 76335, '<td valign="top">Menage trois?</td>', 'Menage trois?', '2011-04-05 20:06:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6375348, 942633, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: It''s been a long time since I''ve seen a selective desaturation look this good. It is perfectly (and eclectically) judged and the tones in the background add considerably to the overall effect. Those browns and the blue complement each other perfectly.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing really<br/> <br/>Overall: How to make gimmicky not. Excellent.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: It''s been a long time since I''ve seen a selective desaturation look this good. It is perfectly (and eclectically) judged and the tones in the background add considerably to the overall effect. Those browns and the blue complement each other perfectly. Critical stuff: Nothing really Overall: How to make gimmicky not. Excellent.', '2011-04-05 20:08:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6375350, 942380, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: A well made image - no doubt about that; it will however make some people uncomfortable. Personally, I think that''s a good thing! The stand-out eyes, slight grain and the lighting/vignette work very well together.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The earrings - they rob the image of some of its power.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very pleased to have seen this. I like unusual portraits and this is right up there.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: A well made image - no doubt about that; it will however make some people uncomfortable. Personally, I think that''s a good thing! The stand-out eyes, slight grain and the lighting/vignette work very well together. Critical stuff: The earrings - they rob the image of some of its power. Overall: Very pleased to have seen this. I like unusual portraits and this is right up there.', '2011-04-05 20:12:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6375357, 943989, 76335, '<td valign="top">Clouds and earth echo each other nicely. I like the muted contrast.</td>', 'Clouds and earth echo each other nicely. I like the muted contrast.', '2011-04-05 20:15:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6375359, 943815, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like the mystery of this image - quite intimate whilst remaining completely anonymous and even discreet. I really want to peek around the door though. I like the distortion on the top of the frame, it gives us a sense of being enclosed. The shoes are a master stroke - in many ways they are the secret to the image; are they there fortuitously or have they been placed. In the answer to that question lies the answer to the story of the scene.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing really - this defies such triviality<br/> <br/>Overall: Made with care. I like that.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like the mystery of this image - quite intimate whilst remaining completely anonymous and even discreet. I really want to peek around the door though. I like the distortion on the top of the frame, it gives us a sense of being enclosed. The shoes are a master stroke - in many ways they are the secret to the image; are they there fortuitously or have they been placed. In the answer to that question lies the answer to the story of the scene. Critical stuff: Nothing really - this defies such triviality Overall: Made with care. I like that.', '2011-04-05 20:19:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6375362, 943923, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Something about this says Pittsburgh to me - I''m not sure why. Perhaps I''m seeing <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=76335" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">bvy</a> tones and extrapolating from that. There seems to be grief here and the thought of that emotion imbues power in the image.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I don''t like the tilt but I would guess the image is stronger for it.<br/> <br/>Overall: Compelling.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Something about this says Pittsburgh to me - I''m not sure why. Perhaps I''m seeing  bvy tones and extrapolating from that. There seems to be grief here and the thought of that emotion imbues power in the image. Critical stuff: I don''t like the tilt but I would guess the image is stronger for it. Overall: Compelling.', '2011-04-05 20:23:30.000000', NULL, 1),
