(6377510, 943915, 108069, '<td valign="top">Quite amazing how the composition framed this perfectly. The breakers in the foreground, obviously, provide a great natural frame for the lighthouse, but the clouds are rolling in and framing it from above in nearly the identical shape. Additional leading lines with the trough running toward the lighthouse. Shipyard cranes in the distance really add depth. Great shot.</td>', 'Quite amazing how the composition framed this perfectly. The breakers in the foreground, obviously, provide a great natural frame for the lighthouse, but the clouds are rolling in and framing it from above in nearly the identical shape. Additional leading lines with the trough running toward the lighthouse. Shipyard cranes in the distance really add depth. Great shot.', '2011-04-07 07:42:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377514, 942412, 86218, '<td valign="top">beautiful simplicity, well processed. I could use this framed. hows a bout adding some life into the road...a dog, cat, runner..something solitairy. Love it 8</td>', 'beautiful simplicity, well processed. I could use this framed. hows a bout adding some life into the road...a dog, cat, runner..something solitairy. Love it 8', '2011-04-07 07:56:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377518, 943314, 108069, '<td valign="top">...and the inhabitants have raced to erect a Stonehenge-like memorial to commemorate said rain. Great depth. I think I would have moved that big center rock to the right or left a bit (in the frame, of course) to get more of a leading line and so it didn''t dominate the foreground, but it''s a small preference. Also, the entire scene seems to slant right, though that may only be an optical illusion. Even if it is, I try to fix those things, as the view is more important than reality. But it''s a very nice photo.</td>', '...and the inhabitants have raced to erect a Stonehenge-like memorial to commemorate said rain. Great depth. I think I would have moved that big center rock to the right or left a bit (in the frame, of course) to get more of a leading line and so it didn''t dominate the foreground, but it''s a small preference. Also, the entire scene seems to slant right, though that may only be an optical illusion. Even if it is, I try to fix those things, as the view is more important than reality. But it''s a very nice photo.', '2011-04-07 08:01:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377669, 939642, 63218, '<td valign="top">Well done, perfectly captured ''classic'' &amp; just-right PP. The fuschia-pink is a  nice surprise, &amp; looks lovely with the sunrise colors in the center. The glowing edges here &amp; there add sparkle. And the light on the top petal is the final touch that adds light to a comp that has very few shadows. Please accept my humble admiration &amp; this Gilded Lily for this gorgeous comp!</td>', 'Well done, perfectly captured ''classic'' & just-right PP. The fuschia-pink is a  nice surprise, & looks lovely with the sunrise colors in the center. The glowing edges here & there add sparkle. And the light on the top petal is the final touch that adds light to a comp that has very few shadows. Please accept my humble admiration & this Gilded Lily for this gorgeous comp!', '2011-04-07 12:13:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377679, 940572, 114225, '<td valign="top">Very nice product shot. The coloring seems to go well with their current style of advertising.</td>', 'Very nice product shot. The coloring seems to go well with their current style of advertising.', '2011-04-07 12:37:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377681, 943927, 114225, '<td valign="top">Absolutely lovely! Perfectly done composition, colors, and exposure.</td>', 'Absolutely lovely! Perfectly done composition, colors, and exposure.', '2011-04-07 12:38:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377682, 943607, 114225, '<td valign="top">I like your choice of high contrast Black and White for this shot. That really sets a mood.</td>', 'I like your choice of high contrast Black and White for this shot. That really sets a mood.', '2011-04-07 12:38:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377683, 942349, 114225, '<td valign="top">Very cool composition of this scene.</td>', 'Very cool composition of this scene.', '2011-04-07 12:39:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377684, 943874, 114225, '<td valign="top">I like how the composition of this makes your eyes start at the head, and natural move down through the rest of the scene.<br/> <br/>One thing I noticed right away, however, is some fairly significant chromatic aberration (see the bright purple on top of the lizard and the right side of the rock?). That is something that can quickly and easily be corrected in post processing, and often gives your image a sharper feel to it.</td>', 'I like how the composition of this makes your eyes start at the head, and natural move down through the rest of the scene. One thing I noticed right away, however, is some fairly significant chromatic aberration (see the bright purple on top of the lizard and the right side of the rock?). That is something that can quickly and easily be corrected in post processing, and often gives your image a sharper feel to it.', '2011-04-07 12:41:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377685, 943921, 114225, '<td valign="top">Beautiful scene. I wish I could be there walking through the trees.</td>', 'Beautiful scene. I wish I could be there walking through the trees.', '2011-04-07 12:42:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377688, 939360, 114225, '<td valign="top">This is a stunning view, perfectly executed. That boat cutting through the mist takes a great photo and makes it spectacular.</td>', 'This is a stunning view, perfectly executed. That boat cutting through the mist takes a great photo and makes it spectacular.', '2011-04-07 12:47:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377689, 940377, 114225, '<td valign="top">Gorgeous colors, reflections, and details. Just a splendid image.</td>', 'Gorgeous colors, reflections, and details. Just a splendid image.', '2011-04-07 12:47:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377762, 939559, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I really really like this. A bunch of Puffins? the coloration is fantastic; pure yet still complex and oh-so-assistive in allowing us to discern the structures. The slightly curved nature of the blur is most compelling - we can almost calculate the radius of curvature from what we see here.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing,<br/> <br/>Overall: There aren''t many people who, having the chance to shoot birds at this distance would choose to create this. I''m ever so glad you did.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I really really like this. A bunch of Puffins? the coloration is fantastic; pure yet still complex and oh-so-assistive in allowing us to discern the structures. The slightly curved nature of the blur is most compelling - we can almost calculate the radius of curvature from what we see here. Critical stuff: Nothing, Overall: There aren''t many people who, having the chance to shoot birds at this distance would choose to create this. I''m ever so glad you did.', '2011-04-07 14:29:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377768, 939400, 69668, '<td valign="top">I love this image.  It is very hard to take an image which doesn''t have a subject and create the mood that you have created.  Very well done.  This image draws me in and creates and emotional response from me.  9</td>', 'I love this image.  It is very hard to take an image which doesn''t have a subject and create the mood that you have created.  Very well done.  This image draws me in and creates and emotional response from me.  9', '2011-04-07 14:37:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377774, 941330, 124346, '<td valign="top">Amazing.</td>', 'Amazing.', '2011-04-07 14:45:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377778, 943822, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: One of those pictures that is more than the sum of its parts. The scene through the window makes for a beautiful abstract landscape in its own right and those streaks of light bottom left are lovely. The walls add to the wonder - as much as by what they obscure as what they show.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing<br/> <br/>Overall: A most pleasing image.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: One of those pictures that is more than the sum of its parts. The scene through the window makes for a beautiful abstract landscape in its own right and those streaks of light bottom left are lovely. The walls add to the wonder - as much as by what they obscure as what they show. Critical stuff: Nothing Overall: A most pleasing image.', '2011-04-07 14:51:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377783, 943753, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I love the rawness of this - with the acid colours (Bleach Bypass??). I really like the curve too - particularly how it causes the disjunction at floor level. The glow of the lights contributes a lot too. The whole effect is rather cinematic, almost like a memory sequence.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I think the colour noise top left is a bit distracting: I think desaturation of the magenta and cyan channels might have reduced this with little negative effect on the rest of the image.<br/> <br/>Overall: A brave shot to enter, but nonetheless one I like a good deal.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I love the rawness of this - with the acid colours (Bleach Bypass??). I really like the curve too - particularly how it causes the disjunction at floor level. The glow of the lights contributes a lot too. The whole effect is rather cinematic, almost like a memory sequence. Critical stuff: I think the colour noise top left is a bit distracting: I think desaturation of the magenta and cyan channels might have reduced this with little negative effect on the rest of the image. Overall: A brave shot to enter, but nonetheless one I like a good deal.', '2011-04-07 14:56:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377787, 942969, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This is a fabulous quirky portrait. The colours are tremendous, particularly the curtains! The pan.... a masterstroke. That decrepit frame... marvellous. The light on his face is just perfect and this contributes to outstanding balance across the frame.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all<br/> <br/>Overall: Magnificent. 10 and a fav.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This is a fabulous quirky portrait. The colours are tremendous, particularly the curtains! The pan.... a masterstroke. That decrepit frame... marvellous. The light on his face is just perfect and this contributes to outstanding balance across the frame. Critical stuff: Nothing at all Overall: Magnificent. 10 and a fav.', '2011-04-07 15:00:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377789, 943931, 124346, '<td valign="top">Is this picture taken at night?  If so that''s amazing.</td>', 'Is this picture taken at night?  If so that''s amazing.', '2011-04-07 15:01:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377794, 943341, 124346, '<td valign="top">I would love to see a picture of the settings of all lights.</td>', 'I would love to see a picture of the settings of all lights.', '2011-04-07 15:07:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377795, 944005, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I really like how this image confounds -where is the light coming from? What is the scale of the image? What is the red thing? What is the black surface? All the better that we don''t know - we can just accept and enjoy the marvellous form and colour.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing<br/> <br/>Overall: Great stuff. It would look great on a wall.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I really like how this image confounds -where is the light coming from? What is the scale of the image? What is the red thing? What is the black surface? All the better that we don''t know - we can just accept and enjoy the marvellous form and colour. Critical stuff: Nothing Overall: Great stuff. It would look great on a wall.', '2011-04-07 15:08:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377803, 943923, 83313, '<td valign="top">There is clearly a story here, but I''m not sure what it is. It could be that she is distraught and he is a strong rock that she can lean on in a time of emotional need. Or, it could be that he is unemotional, uncaring, and cannot sympathize any more than a rock. -OR-, it could be that he is just like me and wants to offer his support, but is a dense male and does not know what to do, so he just stands there.<br/> <br/>Good street photography and deserving of extra pointage for making me stop to look at it and think about what may be going on. <br/> <br/>The overall feel of the shot, including the slight as-shot tilt suggests this could be a <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=76335" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">bvy</a> entry.</td>', 'There is clearly a story here, but I''m not sure what it is. It could be that she is distraught and he is a strong rock that she can lean on in a time of emotional need. Or, it could be that he is unemotional, uncaring, and cannot sympathize any more than a rock. -OR-, it could be that he is just like me and wants to offer his support, but is a dense male and does not know what to do, so he just stands there. Good street photography and deserving of extra pointage for making me stop to look at it and think about what may be going on.  The overall feel of the shot, including the slight as-shot tilt suggests this could be a  bvy entry.', '2011-04-07 15:13:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377804, 943295, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Superb use of a shallow DOF and even better use of SEP2 (am I right - the burn pattern and toning are suggestive of that). The subject matter is most compelling too; the springs with their own form extruding from the fabric below. It all begs the question as to where this mattress (if that''s what it is) is.... the very information we are denied through your low DOF technique.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Although I like burnt edges, I think the transition is a little harsh here.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very nicely seen and made.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Superb use of a shallow DOF and even better use of SEP2 (am I right - the burn pattern and toning are suggestive of that). The subject matter is most compelling too; the springs with their own form extruding from the fabric below. It all begs the question as to where this mattress (if that''s what it is) is.... the very information we are denied through your low DOF technique. Critical stuff: Although I like burnt edges, I think the transition is a little harsh here. Overall: Very nicely seen and made.', '2011-04-07 15:13:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377809, 943342, 83313, '<td valign="top">Love it! An excellent case of recognizing the great shot when it was in front of you and being quick enough to capture it. Faving this one.</td>', 'Love it! An excellent case of recognizing the great shot when it was in front of you and being quick enough to capture it. Faving this one.', '2011-04-07 15:16:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377811, 943963, 83313, '<td valign="top">Looks like a landscape, but it''s nearly an abstract as well. Very nice.</td>', 'Looks like a landscape, but it''s nearly an abstract as well. Very nice.', '2011-04-07 15:17:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377812, 943342, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Fabulously constructed image. Everything is right here and because of that your image, like the bird, soars. The coloration/toning, the light, the exposure, the subjects, the backdrop - it''s difficult to see how it could get better than this.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Umm... no.<br/> <br/>Overall: A DPC great. I''m sure you''ll ribbon. I hope it''s blue. If you haven''t done so already, I''d try this at 1x.com too (if you are so inclined).</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Fabulously constructed image. Everything is right here and because of that your image, like the bird, soars. The coloration/toning, the light, the exposure, the subjects, the backdrop - it''s difficult to see how it could get better than this. Critical stuff: Umm... no. Overall: A DPC great. I''m sure you''ll ribbon. I hope it''s blue. If you haven''t done so already, I''d try this at 1x.com too (if you are so inclined).', '2011-04-07 15:17:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377815, 943327, 83313, '<td valign="top">Wonderful shot. very detailed and great color. My only minor quibble is that I find the composition a bit too centered and static.</td>', 'Wonderful shot. very detailed and great color. My only minor quibble is that I find the composition a bit too centered and static.', '2011-04-07 15:19:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377817, 942715, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I wish I could do work like this! My model work is a bit dull and over-polished compared to this. The colours of the reflections, her pose, the intense eyes, the slightly soft focus, the grain - they all exude confidence in your work. Great stuff.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The framing / cropping on the left.... perhaps a bit more would be better, here, by nearly catching all of her, the slight clipping draws the eye away from where it belongs.<br/> <br/>Overall: Superb work.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I wish I could do work like this! My model work is a bit dull and over-polished compared to this. The colours of the reflections, her pose, the intense eyes, the slightly soft focus, the grain - they all exude confidence in your work. Great stuff. Critical stuff: The framing / cropping on the left.... perhaps a bit more would be better, here, by nearly catching all of her, the slight clipping draws the eye away from where it belongs. Overall: Superb work.', '2011-04-07 15:21:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377822, 942801, 83313, '<td valign="top">I like this, but I''m not sure if the person is holding another person in his arms, or something else. Maybe wearing a cape? It''s hard to tell but I think that is part of the story this is trying to convey and I''m just not getting that part of it.</td>', 'I like this, but I''m not sure if the person is holding another person in his arms, or something else. Maybe wearing a cape? It''s hard to tell but I think that is part of the story this is trying to convey and I''m just not getting that part of it.', '2011-04-07 15:23:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377824, 944035, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: My what a choice you''ve made to submit this. I bet you''re getting killed and I bet you don''t mind at all! I love her wild hair and the sharp focus on her eye and the rule of thirds composition.... like you''ve approached it like a real portrait, with the limbs and torso being ''posed'' in a very real way. I really like that bronze coloration too and the way that you''ve processed and captured the light in a way that makes the highlights a feature in their own right. I also think the negative space at the top is inspired.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing<br/> <br/>Overall: I could see this in a gallery and I for one would be transfixed. Excellent</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: My what a choice you''ve made to submit this. I bet you''re getting killed and I bet you don''t mind at all! I love her wild hair and the sharp focus on her eye and the rule of thirds composition.... like you''ve approached it like a real portrait, with the limbs and torso being ''posed'' in a very real way. I really like that bronze coloration too and the way that you''ve processed and captured the light in a way that makes the highlights a feature in their own right. I also think the negative space at the top is inspired. Critical stuff: Nothing Overall: I could see this in a gallery and I for one would be transfixed. Excellent', '2011-04-07 15:25:17.000000', NULL, 1),
