(6377993, 943715, 76335, '<td valign="top">I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1069301" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">see recent forum thread</a>). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5.<br/> <br/>A nicely executed candid and good job with the lighting. A five and not a six because this feels like a family snapshot. And don''t get me wrong -- there''s no shame in family snapshots. But I suspect this particular one offers more to, say, family than to a stranger in a photo contest. <br/> <br/>So there you go!</td>', 'I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5. A nicely executed candid and good job with the lighting. A five and not a six because this feels like a family snapshot. And don''t get me wrong -- there''s no shame in family snapshots. But I suspect this particular one offers more to, say, family than to a stranger in a photo contest.  So there you go!', '2011-04-07 19:16:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6377999, 939834, 76335, '<td valign="top">I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1069301" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">see recent forum thread</a>). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5.<br/> <br/>Beautifully composed, and technically speaking, it''s just about perfect. Why a five and not a six? I feel like I''ve seen this before. And will see it again. Perhaps if I were a mountain or landscape photographer, I''d feel differently. And maybe that''s just it. It''s just not my cup of tea. I''m attracted to things with more mystery, more ambiguity. I do like black and white landscapes, but I feel like this one needs more black. <br/> <br/>Anyway...</td>', 'I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5. Beautifully composed, and technically speaking, it''s just about perfect. Why a five and not a six? I feel like I''ve seen this before. And will see it again. Perhaps if I were a mountain or landscape photographer, I''d feel differently. And maybe that''s just it. It''s just not my cup of tea. I''m attracted to things with more mystery, more ambiguity. I do like black and white landscapes, but I feel like this one needs more black.  Anyway...', '2011-04-07 19:30:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6378002, 941316, 76335, '<td valign="top">I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1069301" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">see recent forum thread</a>). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5.<br/> <br/>I like that you were able to take the viewer right into the action. Technically, it''s very good -- the light (which I suspect was challenging), the focus, etc. Why just a five? I don''t feel like I''m seeing a real moment of activity here. Feels like a moment between moments. Also, the player in focus is blocked by Chara there. And there''s a clipped stick off to the right. Maybe I just don''t watch enough hockey...</td>', 'I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5. I like that you were able to take the viewer right into the action. Technically, it''s very good -- the light (which I suspect was challenging), the focus, etc. Why just a five? I don''t feel like I''m seeing a real moment of activity here. Feels like a moment between moments. Also, the player in focus is blocked by Chara there. And there''s a clipped stick off to the right. Maybe I just don''t watch enough hockey...', '2011-04-07 19:34:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6378006, 943909, 76335, '<td valign="top">I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1069301" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">see recent forum thread</a>). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5.<br/> <br/>I very much like the compositon -- the way the winding road takes us in and out of the perpindicular trees. The colors are pleasing too. Why just a five? Plain and simple -- I don''t like the processing. It feels like it got a dose of Topaz or HDR, and I''m not a fan of that look. However, I appreciate that you used it in moderation, and at the end of the day, I still rather like this image. <br/> <br/>Now you know.</td>', 'I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5. I very much like the compositon -- the way the winding road takes us in and out of the perpindicular trees. The colors are pleasing too. Why just a five? Plain and simple -- I don''t like the processing. It feels like it got a dose of Topaz or HDR, and I''m not a fan of that look. However, I appreciate that you used it in moderation, and at the end of the day, I still rather like this image.  Now you know.', '2011-04-07 19:40:29.000000', NULL, 1),
