(6378179, 940324, 76335, '<td valign="top">I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1069301" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">see recent forum thread</a>). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5.<br/> <br/>Her expression is beautiful, and the warm sepia processing with the blurred background are spectacular. It has a vintage feel to it. As such, I admit to being a little disappointed at seeing a very modern toy in her hands (I have a small screen and had to scroll down to find it). In fact, I didn''t realize it was a camera until I saw your title. <br/> <br/>Is this your daughter? My personal quibbles aside, this is an endearing candid, something to be proud of and share.</td>', 'I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5. Her expression is beautiful, and the warm sepia processing with the blurred background are spectacular. It has a vintage feel to it. As such, I admit to being a little disappointed at seeing a very modern toy in her hands (I have a small screen and had to scroll down to find it). In fact, I didn''t realize it was a camera until I saw your title.  Is this your daughter? My personal quibbles aside, this is an endearing candid, something to be proud of and share.', '2011-04-07 22:57:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6378181, 943977, 115307, '<td valign="top">Wow, I really like this. The matching sillhoettes in the foreground and background are really interesting. I love the sunset colors and the violinists, the two mesh really well. 9</td>', 'Wow, I really like this. The matching sillhoettes in the foreground and background are really interesting. I love the sunset colors and the violinists, the two mesh really well. 9', '2011-04-07 22:58:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(6378186, 943086, 115307, '<td valign="top">Very nice angle and lighting. I would have cloned out the hairs that are on the knee. Even though they are strands from the head, it gives the illusion of really long leg hair, which is gross. I love the composition, with the diagonal foot giving a means out of the frame. 7</td>', 'Very nice angle and lighting. I would have cloned out the hairs that are on the knee. Even though they are strands from the head, it gives the illusion of really long leg hair, which is gross. I love the composition, with the diagonal foot giving a means out of the frame. 7', '2011-04-07 23:01:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6378190, 940726, 76335, '<td valign="top">I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1069301" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">see recent forum thread</a>). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5.<br/> <br/>Love the scene you chose, but I was a little unsure about the composition. The right side has some dead weight (the wall). Also, the eye (my eye anyway)jumps to the window and from there, the ceiling, which I suspect is most awesome, but alas, very little of it is visible. I also feel like some foreground elements of some interest might have also been cropped, but I''m not sure. A portrait view of the same scene might have put you into my land of six. <br/> <br/>So now you know. And if you didn''t get a six from me, it might interest you to know that this is my nine thousandth comment here.</td>', 'I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5. Love the scene you chose, but I was a little unsure about the composition. The right side has some dead weight (the wall). Also, the eye (my eye anyway)jumps to the window and from there, the ceiling, which I suspect is most awesome, but alas, very little of it is visible. I also feel like some foreground elements of some interest might have also been cropped, but I''m not sure. A portrait view of the same scene might have put you into my land of six.  So now you know. And if you didn''t get a six from me, it might interest you to know that this is my nine thousandth comment here.', '2011-04-07 23:03:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6378191, 943977, 76335, '<td valign="top">I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1069301" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">see recent forum thread</a>). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5.<br/> <br/>I do like this. I wonder if it''s candid. A slightly better angle for your subject, something that showed him passionately engaging bow to strings in silhouette, might have put this over the top into six or seven territory for me. If it''s candid though (as I suspect it is) then the opportunity just might not have presented itself.</td>', 'I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5. I do like this. I wonder if it''s candid. A slightly better angle for your subject, something that showed him passionately engaging bow to strings in silhouette, might have put this over the top into six or seven territory for me. If it''s candid though (as I suspect it is) then the opportunity just might not have presented itself.', '2011-04-07 23:04:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(6378193, 943751, 76335, '<td valign="top">I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1069301" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">see recent forum thread</a>). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5.<br/> <br/>I like the almost abstract presentation of this. Why a five and not a six? The lighting, especially in the distance (the glacier, I suppose), feels a bit harsh. I think shooting earlier or later in the day might have produced more dramatic shadows and offered a lot more options. Still, it''s very compelling, and I like the cool tones and quirky geological forms.</td>', 'I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5. I like the almost abstract presentation of this. Why a five and not a six? The lighting, especially in the distance (the glacier, I suppose), feels a bit harsh. I think shooting earlier or later in the day might have produced more dramatic shadows and offered a lot more options. Still, it''s very compelling, and I like the cool tones and quirky geological forms.', '2011-04-07 23:05:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(6378197, 944018, 76335, '<td valign="top">I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1069301" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">see recent forum thread</a>). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5. <br/> <br/>Really beautiful. Feels infrared and maybe it is. The colors do suggest the transitional time that is March or early spring. Why a five and not a six? I have to admit that I could easily have given this a six in a different frame of mind. For the purposes of this exercise, I won''t bump it. Anyway, I feel like some more separation in the trees to make them pop a bit would have helped this along. Maybe it''s the size of the image on my small screen that reduces them to a (mostly) white mass. But I''m trying to look past that.</td>', 'I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5.  Really beautiful. Feels infrared and maybe it is. The colors do suggest the transitional time that is March or early spring. Why a five and not a six? I have to admit that I could easily have given this a six in a different frame of mind. For the purposes of this exercise, I won''t bump it. Anyway, I feel like some more separation in the trees to make them pop a bit would have helped this along. Maybe it''s the size of the image on my small screen that reduces them to a (mostly) white mass. But I''m trying to look past that.', '2011-04-07 23:06:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6378199, 941505, 76335, '<td valign="top">I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (<a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/forum.php?action=read&amp;FORUM_THREAD_ID=1069301" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">see recent forum thread</a>). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5.<br/> <br/>A good action shot and I do like surf photography. Why not a six? I think seeing some wave (or a more clearly defined wave -- he''s not surfing on air, I realize) along with the surfer would have made this shot stronger. Still very good.</td>', 'I am participating in the "Why a ''5'' not a ''6''?" commenting activity (see recent forum thread). Viewers are asked to leave a comment with some of their votes of ''5'' letting the photographer know why, for them, it fell short of a vote of ''6''. If you have found this comment useful, you may wish to offer some of your own to those images where you vote 5. A good action shot and I do like surf photography. Why not a six? I think seeing some wave (or a more clearly defined wave -- he''s not surfing on air, I realize) along with the surfer would have made this shot stronger. Still very good.', '2011-04-07 23:07:28.000000', NULL, 1),
