(6379849, 943179, 93283, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ikopanas:</b></div><hr/><i> I did not vote this one high, mostly because of the light! I d prefer the shadows to be less shadowed and the lit area on the shot to be less highlighted. And for sure the right area of the shot gives me the feeling of a line that seperates the environment! Hope this helps! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thank you very much for stopping by to comment on my image. I agree with everything you said and figured that the harsh light was the reason for lower voting. I also noticed the line on the right side of the image and figured somebody would request the proof to see if I shopped it that way. I seem to get that line allot when shooting stuff like this where sawgrass meets water. I''ve got to figure out a way to fix that... Thanks again...</td>', 'Originally posted by ikopanas: I did not vote this one high, mostly because of the light! I d prefer the shadows to be less shadowed and the lit area on the shot to be less highlighted. And for sure the right area of the shot gives me the feeling of a line that seperates the environment! Hope this helps!   Thank you very much for stopping by to comment on my image. I agree with everything you said and figured that the harsh light was the reason for lower voting. I also noticed the line on the right side of the image and figured somebody would request the proof to see if I shopped it that way. I seem to get that line allot when shooting stuff like this where sawgrass meets water. I''ve got to figure out a way to fix that... Thanks again...', '2011-04-08 23:55:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6379853, 944032, 68504, '<td valign="top">Why does this make me think of Georgia O''Keefe?  Just enough meat on the bone, no fat.</td>', 'Why does this make me think of Georgia O''Keefe?  Just enough meat on the bone, no fat.', '2011-04-08 23:57:23.000000', NULL, 0),
